  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-11-20T05:59:41.230Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "What it says on the tin, really. I have two seats on my avatar, set to toggles, but if someone doesn't completely show my avatar, usually due to their safety settings showing my avatar model and little else, my seats appear on to those who don't have my avatar shown. The seats are set to toggle ON when I set them to in my radial menu, but otherwise be 100% off\n\nThis means that strangers can sit on my avatar's seats, which are both lined up so they are behind my head, where I cannot see them easily, meaning that the stranger(s) could be doing gross things to me against my will where I cannot see them.\n\nI've spoken to the base's maker, and he's stumped as to why and believes it to be a VRC related bug.\n\nThose in the official Discord server believe it to be easily fixed by animating the seat so that when not in use it's a billion miles away from me, but the main feature I'm hung up on is that I SHOULDN'T have to edit how my animations work just because strangers can access my seats when my radial menu says they are off and they don't show my avatar fully.\n\nPlease fix this, as having strangers invade my personal space by sitting on seats they shouldn't be able to see in the first place is both aggravating and a bit anxiety educing.\n\nIn fact, this issue could be used to HARASS people and cause untold anxiety and stress.\n\nAnd I will state this before someone requests I try it, letting strangers activate my headpat features is why I won't turn off avatar interacts.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this, as this came about because a stranger insisted on invading my personal space by sitting on one of my seats while calling me \"horsie,\" and I've just had enough.",
